{"authorityRole":"external_auditor","by":"buger","candidateKey":"","candidateKind":"","changeKey":"pr/9056","createdAt":"2026-10-02T18:14:22Z","decision":"accept_change","decisionDigest":"sha256:e1e01610c2262121175432e55b5693b9a144341163605d58533f621034868f30","decisionId":"rdec-955b6f758a2fe124fbb01b54a4e2f5ee","identitySource":"github_login","packageDigest":"sha256:fc915b4c9331e72a8ad68dc2217cbc723b09fcd055d96b67e4b6cd5f386fd849","packageIdentity":"epkg-00b5e30fb9fbf70b1815915dd2bb59fdd56e01f24941485f23653fec60619c01","prNumber":"9056","reason":"Recommend accepting: a new summon now answers the earlier waiting caller as cancelled instead of leaving it stuck (#9057), and the head b7bd59c4 also fixes the burst race found on the first commit. On a live Omarchy session, a burst of 20 summons left 19 callers stuck on quattro c05d9019, 7 to 12 on the first commit 0b4fe29, and 0 on b7bd59c4, in all 6 runs. The two-summon case exits cleanly, and a real selection still returns its value. A headless regression test for overlapping requests fails on both older trees and passes 8/8 on this head. One gap remains outside this PR: if the menu process dies after a summon, the caller still waits forever (tracked on #9057).","repo":"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy","schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-decision.v1","scope":"change"}
